"""Food & harvest: what gardens, orchards and kitchens have too much of, from temperate
to tropical climates (courgettes, apples, mangoes, eggs, jam), and what is saved from
being thrown away (bread, a box of peanut butter past its date, a sack of rice).

Each entry: (slug, broader thing's slug, gift category slug, en, de, es, fr, other
names in any language separated by "|"). A broader thing goes before the narrower ones;
names are singular where food is counted, else as it is said ("Rice", "Pulses"). Other
names hold the plural, regional words (Austrian: Paradeiser, Marille, Karfiol; Swiss:
Rüebli; Latin American: palta, durazno, frijoles) and names from where it grows, for
search. Slugs start with "food-", to keep apart from the seed and plant vocabulary's
("apple" is the tree, "food-apples" the fruit). Food is always in "Food & Preserves" too
(Listing.thing_categories)."""

